IMPORT prelude

-- Migration Act 1958 (Cth), with the Migration Regulations 1994 -- what the visa applicant and visa holder meet.
--
-- SEAT: the visa applicant and visa holder -- Priya, an Indian national married to an Australian citizen, on her way
-- from a student visa through a Bridging A and a temporary partner visa (subclass 820) to a permanent one (subclass
-- 801), then travelling; and the machine-learning engineer from Chennai whom Jarrah sponsors on a Skills in Demand
-- visa (subclass 482). "Do I need a visa, which one can I get, may I work, may I leave and come back, and what can
-- take it away?" Every question below is phrased as that person would ask it, on facts that person could state.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Act: lawful and unlawful non-citizens (ss 13, 14) and the visa needed to travel (s 42);
-- visas and their kinds (ss 29, 30); spouse and de facto partner (ss 5F, 5CB); the decision on an application
-- (s 65); bridging visas (ss 72, 73); a visa ceasing when another comes into effect, or when its holder leaves or
-- its travel period ends (s 82(2), (3), (5), (6), (8)); re-entry (ss 79, 81(2)); conditions (s 41); cancellation under
-- s 116 and the bar for a permanent visa holder in Australia (ss 116(1), (1AA)-(1AC), (2), 117(2)), with notice
-- (ss 119, 128); my sponsor's approval, my nomination and what a sponsor risks for breaking an obligation (s 5(1)
-- "approved work sponsor", ss 140E, 140GB(2), 140H, 140Q, 486R(5)); paying for sponsorship (s 245AS); an employer
-- allowing a non-citizen to work (ss 245AB, 245AC, 245AG).
-- Regulations: reg 1.03 ("Australian permanent resident", "long-term partner relationship", "core skills income
-- threshold", "specialist skills income threshold"); reg 2.72(8), (15) (the salary test for a nomination); reg 2.75
-- (when a nomination's approval ceases); regs 2.79, 2.80, 2.87 (the sponsorship obligations that protect the worker);
-- reg 5.42A (indexation of the thresholds); Schedule 1 items 1128 (Return (Residence)), 1214C (Partner (Temporary)),
-- 1240 (Skills in Demand), 1301 (Bridging A); Schedule 2 Parts 010 (Bridging A), 155 (Five Year Resident Return),
-- 482 (Skills in Demand, Specialist Skills and Core Skills streams), 801 (Partner) and 820 (Partner); Schedule 8
-- conditions 8105, 8501 and 8607.
--
-- Edition: Migration Act 1958, Compilation No. 171, compilation date 4 June 2026 ("Includes amendments: Act No. 75,
-- 2025"; register id C2026C00232), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1958A00062.txt (retrieved
-- 2026-09-22). Regulations used: Migration Regulations 1994 (F1996B03551), Compilation No. 289, compilation date
-- 2 October 2026 (includes amendments F2026L01347; register id F2026C01017, 4 volumes joined), as deposited at
-- ../../../migration-regulations-1994/registers/source-bundle/F1996B03551.txt (retrieved 2026-10-20).
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Every visa subclass not named above (visitor, student criteria, other partner and skilled visas,
-- protection visas, Bridging B to F); the 482 Labour Agreement stream beyond saying that the salary test of reg
-- 2.72(15) does not reach it; the public interest criteria (Schedule 4: health, character, debts) and the special
-- return criteria (Schedule 5), each asked as one fact; Schedule 3 criteria (asked as a fact); the 801/820
-- application charges (Schedule 1 item 1124B has ten tables keyed on old transitional cases; not encoded); the
-- instruments that set the occupation lists, the market salary method, the high-earnings exemption amount, the
-- language tests and the indexed thresholds (INPUTS, with the floors the Regulations guarantee); the sponsor's own
-- approval criteria (prescribed for s 140E), labour market testing itself (s 140GBA) and the reg 2.72 criteria other
-- than the salary test (each one input); sponsorship obligations other than regs 2.79, 2.80 and 2.87 (record-keeping,
-- notifying, cooperating with inspectors); sponsor sanctions (ss 140K-140M);
-- character cancellation (s 501) and every cancellation power other than s 116; merits and judicial review;
-- detention and removal; the Minister's personal and non-compellable powers. The value of a penalty unit is set by
-- the Crimes Act 1914, not this Act.
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice.
-- See NOTES.md.

§ `Migration Act 1958 and Migration Regulations 1994 -- the visa applicant's and holder's questions`

§§ `ss 13, 14, 42 -- do I need a visa`

-- s 13(1): "A non-citizen in the migration zone who holds a visa that is in effect is a lawful non-citizen." (2): an
-- allowed inhabitant of the Protected Zone in a protected area for traditional activities is also lawful.
-- s 14(1): "A non-citizen in the migration zone who is not a lawful non-citizen is an unlawful non-citizen."
@export Am I a lawful non-citizen (s 13)?
GIVEN `I am an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen
      `I am in the migration zone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in Australia (the migration zone)
      `I hold a visa that is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a visa that is in effect, including a bridging visa
      `I am a Protected Zone inhabitant there for traditional activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an allowed inhabitant of the Torres Strait Protected Zone in a protected area for traditional activities
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a lawful non-citizen` IF
        (NOT `I am an Australian citizen`)
    AND (    (`I am in the migration zone` AND `I hold a visa that is in effect`)
         OR  `I am a Protected Zone inhabitant there for traditional activities`)

@export Am I an unlawful non-citizen (s 14)?
GIVEN `I am an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen
      `I am in the migration zone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in Australia (the migration zone)
      `I hold a visa that is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a visa that is in effect, including a bridging visa
      `I am a Protected Zone inhabitant there for traditional activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an allowed inhabitant of the Torres Strait Protected Zone in a protected area for traditional activities
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an unlawful non-citizen` IF
        (NOT `I am an Australian citizen`)
    AND `I am in the migration zone`
    AND (NOT (`Am I a lawful non-citizen` `I am an Australian citizen` `I am in the migration zone` `I hold a visa that is in effect` `I am a Protected Zone inhabitant there for traditional activities`))

-- s 42(1): "a non-citizen must not travel to Australia without a visa that is in effect." (2A)(a): not "if the
-- travel is by a New Zealand citizen who holds and produces a New Zealand passport that is in force"; (2): not an
-- allowed inhabitant of the Protected Zone travelling to a protected area for traditional activities. The other
-- exceptions in (2A) and (3) concern people brought to Australia by officials and are not encoded.
@export Must I hold a visa to travel to Australia (s 42)?
GIVEN `I am an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian citizen
      `I am a New Zealand citizen with a New Zealand passport in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a New Zealand citizen who holds and will produce a New Zealand passport that is in force
      `I am a Protected Zone inhabitant travelling for traditional activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an allowed inhabitant of the Protected Zone travelling to a protected area for traditional activities
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I hold a visa to travel to Australia` IF
        (NOT `I am an Australian citizen`)
    AND (NOT `I am a New Zealand citizen with a New Zealand passport in force`)
    AND (NOT `I am a Protected Zone inhabitant travelling for traditional activities`)

§§ `ss 29, 30 -- what kind of visa do I hold`

-- s 29(1): a visa is permission to "(a) travel to and enter Australia; (b) remain in Australia", or both.
-- s 30(1): "a visa, to be known as a permanent visa, to remain indefinitely." (2): "a visa, to be known as a temporary
-- visa, to remain: (a) during a specified period; or (b) until a specified event happens; or (c) while the holder has a
-- specified status."
DECLARE `Permission to remain` IS ONE OF
    `indefinitely`
    `during a specified period`
    `until a specified event happens`
    `while I have a specified status`

@export Is my visa a permanent visa (s 30)?
GIVEN `how long my visa lets me remain` IS A `Permission to remain` @desc How long your visa lets you stay in Australia
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my visa permanent` IF
    CONSIDER `how long my visa lets me remain`
    WHEN `indefinitely` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 5F, 5CB -- am I my partner's spouse or de facto partner`

-- s 5F(2): "persons are in a married relationship if: (a) they are married to each other under a marriage that is valid
-- for the purposes of this Act; and (b) they have a mutual commitment to a shared life as a married couple to the
-- exclusion of all others; and (c) the relationship between them is genuine and continuing; and (d) they: (i) live
-- together; or (ii) do not live separately and apart on a permanent basis." Validity (s 12) comes from Part VA of the
-- Marriage Act 1961: a borrowed term, asked as a fact.
-- s 5CB(2): a de facto relationship is the same three conditions without the marriage, "(d) they are not related by
-- family".
DECLARE `Our relationship` HAS
    `we are married under a marriage valid for the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `we are committed to a shared life to the exclusion of all others` IS A BOOLEAN
    `our relationship is genuine and continuing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `we live together` IS A BOOLEAN
    `we live separately and apart on a permanent basis` IS A BOOLEAN
    `we are related by family` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `r` IS AN `Our relationship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `we share a life under s 5F or 5CB` IF
        `r`'s `we are committed to a shared life to the exclusion of all others`
    AND `r`'s `our relationship is genuine and continuing`
    AND (`r`'s `we live together` OR (NOT `r`'s `we live separately and apart on a permanent basis`))

@export Am I my partner's spouse (s 5F)?
GIVEN `r` IS AN `Our relationship` @desc Facts about you and your partner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I my partner's spouse` IF
    `r`'s `we are married under a marriage valid for the Act` AND `we share a life under s 5F or 5CB` `r`

@export Am I my partner's de facto partner (s 5CB)?
GIVEN `r` IS AN `Our relationship` @desc Facts about you and your partner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I my partner's de facto partner` IF
        (NOT `Am I my partner's spouse` `r`)
    AND `we share a life under s 5F or 5CB` `r`
    AND (NOT `r`'s `we are related by family`)

§§ `s 65 -- the decision on my application`

-- s 65(1): "Subject to sections 84 and 86, after considering a valid application for a visa, the Minister: (a) if
-- satisfied that: (i) the health criteria for it (if any) have been satisfied; and (ii) the other criteria for it
-- prescribed by this Act or the regulations have been satisfied; and (iii) the grant of the visa is not prevented by
-- section 40 ..., 501 ... or any other provision ...; and (iv) any amount of visa application charge payable ... has
-- been paid; is to grant the visa; or (b) if not so satisfied, is to refuse to grant the visa." A judgment handed to
-- the Minister: each limb is an input ("if the Minister is satisfied ..."). Treating ss 84 (suspension) and 86 (caps)
-- as leaving the application undecided is an INFERENCE from "Subject to".
DECLARE `Decision` IS ONE OF
    `the visa must be granted`
    `the visa must be refused`
    `no decision yet`

GIVEN `a valid application has been considered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `processing is suspended or capped` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied the criteria are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `nothing prevents the grant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charge is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Decision`
DECIDE `the s 65 decision` IS
    IF (NOT `a valid application has been considered`) OR `processing is suspended or capped`
    THEN `no decision yet`
    ELSE IF `the Minister is satisfied the criteria are met` AND `nothing prevents the grant` AND `the charge is paid`
         THEN `the visa must be granted`
         ELSE `the visa must be refused`

§§ `Sch 1 item 1214C; Sch 2 Part 820 -- the temporary partner visa (Priya, d033)`

-- Sch 1 item 1214C(3): "(a) Application must be made at the same time and place as an application for a Partner
-- (Residence) (Class BS) visa. ... (c) Applicant must be in Australia, but not in immigration clearance." (2): "Visa
-- application charge: Nil" -- the charge is paid on the Class BS application.
@export May I make a valid application for the temporary partner visa in Australia (Sch 1 item 1214C)?
GIVEN `I apply for the permanent partner visa at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lodge the Partner (Residence) (Class BS) application at the same time and place
      `I am in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in Australia when you apply
      `I am in immigration clearance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are still in immigration clearance at the airport or port
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply for the temporary partner visa in Australia` IF
    `I apply for the permanent partner visa at the same time` AND `I am in Australia` AND (NOT `I am in immigration clearance`)

-- 820.211(1): "The applicant: (a) is not the holder of a Subclass 771 (Transit) visa; and (b) meets the requirements of
-- subclause (2) ...". (2): "(a) the applicant is the spouse or de facto partner of a person who: (i) is an Australian
-- citizen, an Australian permanent resident or an eligible New Zealand citizen; and (ii) is not prohibited by subclause
-- (2B) from being a sponsoring partner; and (c) the applicant is sponsored: (i) if the applicant's spouse or de facto
-- partner has turned 18 -- by the spouse or de facto partner; or (ii) ... by a parent or guardian of the spouse ...;
-- and (d) in the case of an applicant who is not the holder of a substantive visa -- either: ... (ii) the applicant
-- satisfies Schedule 3 criteria 3001, 3003 and 3004, unless the Minister is satisfied that there are compelling reasons
-- for not applying those criteria." The diplomatic and SOFA route in (d)(i), and subclauses (5)-(9) (prospective
-- marriage visa holders), are not encoded.
DECLARE `Partner application` HAS
    `I hold a transit visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my partner is an Australian citizen, permanent resident or eligible New Zealand citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my partner is barred from sponsoring by 820.211(2B)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am sponsored by my partner, or by their parent or guardian if they are under 18` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I hold a substantive visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I meet Schedule 3 criteria 3001, 3003 and 3004 or the Minister waives them` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Do I meet the temporary partner visa criteria when I apply (cl 820.211)?
GIVEN `r` IS AN `Our relationship` @desc Facts about you and your partner
      `p` IS A `Partner application` @desc Facts about your application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the temporary partner visa criteria when I apply` IF
        (NOT `p`'s `I hold a transit visa`)
    AND (`Am I my partner's spouse` `r` OR `Am I my partner's de facto partner` `r`)
    AND `p`'s `my partner is an Australian citizen, permanent resident or eligible New Zealand citizen`
    AND (NOT `p`'s `my partner is barred from sponsoring by 820.211(2B)`)
    AND `p`'s `I am sponsored by my partner, or by their parent or guardian if they are under 18`
    AND (`p`'s `I hold a substantive visa` OR `p`'s `I meet Schedule 3 criteria 3001, 3003 and 3004 or the Minister waives them`)

-- At decision, 820.221(1): the applicant "(a) continues to meet the requirements of the applicable subclause; or (b)
-- meets the requirements of subclause (2) or (3)" -- (2) the sponsoring partner has died and the Minister is satisfied
-- the relationship would have continued; (3) the relationship has ceased and the applicant or a dependent child "has
-- experienced family violence committed by the sponsoring partner", or there is a child custody, contact or
-- maintenance link with the sponsoring partner. 820.221(4), 820.221A: "the sponsorship has been approved by the
-- Minister and is still in force". 820.223, 820.226: public interest criteria 4001, 4002, 4003, 4004, 4007, 4009,
-- 4019 (if 18 at application), 4020 and 4021 -- asked as one fact.
@export Must my temporary partner visa be granted (s 65 with cll 820.221-820.226)?
GIVEN `a valid application has been considered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a valid application of yours has been considered
      `processing is suspended or capped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether processing is suspended (s 84) or the cap has been reached (s 86)
      `I still meet the 820.211 requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you still meet the requirements you met when you applied
      `my partner died, or we separated after family violence or with a child order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, if the relationship has ended, it ended in one of the ways cl 820.221(2) or (3) allows, as the Minister is satisfied
      `my sponsorship is approved and in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister has approved your partner's sponsorship and it is still in force
      `I meet the public interest criteria` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you meet the health, character and other public interest criteria, as the Minister is satisfied
      `the charge is paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the visa application charge on the partner application has been paid
GIVETH A `Decision`
DECIDE `Must my temporary partner visa be granted` IS
    `the s 65 decision` `a valid application has been considered` `processing is suspended or capped`
        (    (`I still meet the 820.211 requirements` OR `my partner died, or we separated after family violence or with a child order`)
         AND `my sponsorship is approved and in force`
         AND `I meet the public interest criteria`)
        TRUE
        `the charge is paid`

-- 820.511: "Temporary visa permitting the holder to travel to and enter Australia until: (a) the holder is notified
-- that his or her application for a Subclass 801 (Partner) visa has been decided; or (b) that application is
-- withdrawn." 820.6: "Conditions: Nil." 801.6: "Conditions: Nil."
@export Does my partner visa (subclass 820 or 801) carry any condition, including a limit on work (cll 820.6, 801.6)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my partner visa carry any condition` IS FALSE

§§ `ss 72, 73; Sch 1 item 1301; Sch 2 Part 010; Sch 8 condition 8105 -- the Bridging A visa while I wait (Priya, d033)`

-- 010.211(2): "(a) the applicant has made, in Australia, a valid application for a substantive visa of a kind that can
-- be granted if the applicant is in Australia; and (b) that application has not been finally determined; and (c) he or
-- she held a substantive visa at the time that application was made; and (d) either: (i) he or she has applied for a
-- bridging visa in respect of that application; or (ii) a bridging visa can be granted ... under regulation 2.21B."
-- 010.221: the criterion continues at decision. 010.411: "The applicant must be in Australia, but not in immigration
-- clearance." s 72(1)(a): an eligible non-citizen includes one who "has been immigration cleared"; s 73: the Minister
-- "may grant" a bridging visa to an eligible non-citizen who meets the criteria. Subclauses 010.211(3)-(6) (judicial
-- review; compelling need to work; Class BC cases) are not encoded.
@export Do I meet the Bridging A visa criteria while my application is decided (s 73; cll 010.211, 010.411)?
GIVEN `I applied in Australia for a visa that can be granted in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made a valid application, in Australia, for a substantive visa that can be granted while you are in Australia
      `that application is not finally determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that application is still undecided
      `I held a substantive visa when I applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you held a substantive visa (not a bridging visa) when you made that application
      `I applied for a bridging visa with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied for a bridging visa in respect of that application
      `I am in Australia and not in immigration clearance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in Australia and past immigration clearance
      `I have been immigration cleared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were immigration cleared when you entered Australia
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the Bridging A criteria` IF
        `I applied in Australia for a visa that can be granted in Australia`
    AND `that application is not finally determined`
    AND `I held a substantive visa when I applied`
    AND `I applied for a bridging visa with it`
    AND `I am in Australia and not in immigration clearance`
    AND `I have been immigration cleared`

-- 010.511(1)(b): the visa permits the holder to remain until "(i) if the Minister's decision ... is to grant a visa --
-- the grant of the visa; or (ii) if the Minister's decision ... is to refuse to grant a visa and subclause (1A) does not
-- apply ... -- 35 days after the Minister makes the decision; or (iiaa) ... and subclause (1A) applies ... -- the time
-- the Minister makes the decision; ... (iii) if ... the ART makes a decision on the holder's application for merits
-- review ... -- 35 days after the ART makes the decision; ... (v) if the holder withdraws his or her application ...
-- -- 35 days after that withdrawal". (1A): the refusal was for failing public interest criterion 4003(b) or 4003A.
DECLARE `What happened to my application` IS ONE OF
    `it was granted`
    `it was refused`
    `it was refused for failing public interest criterion 4003(b) or 4003A`
    `the ART decided my review of a refusal`
    `I withdrew it`

@export How many days after the decision may I stay on my Bridging A visa (cl 010.511)?
GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened to my application` @desc What happened to the application your Bridging A visa was granted on
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days after the decision may I stay on my Bridging A visa` IS
    CONSIDER `what happened`
    WHEN `it was granted` THEN 0
    WHEN `it was refused for failing public interest criterion 4003(b) or 4003A` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 35

-- 010.611(4): "In any other case: whichever of conditions 8101, 8102, 8103, 8104, 8105, 8107, 8108, 8111, 8112, 8114,
-- 8115, 8539, 8547, 8549, 8607 and 8608 applies to: (a) the visa held by the holder: (i) at the time of application".
-- 010.611(1): "Nil" for a holder who "(a) satisfies the criterion in subclause 010.211(4)" (compelling need to work)
-- or "(c) is a person in a class of persons specified by the Minister by an instrument in writing for this
-- paragraph". The instrument is not deposited: whether I am in its class is an input. Condition 8202 (enrolment) and
-- 8501 (health insurance) are not in the list, so they do not carry over.
@export Does my Bridging A visa carry the work limit of the visa I held when I applied (cl 010.611)?
GIVEN `my last visa had a work condition in the 010.611(4) list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the visa you held when you applied had a work condition such as 8104 or 8105 (a student visa has 8105)
      `I am in a class the Minister specified for 010.611(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in a class of persons the Minister has specified by instrument for a Bridging A without conditions
      `I was granted it for a compelling need to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your Bridging A was granted because the Minister was satisfied you have a compelling need to work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my Bridging A carry my last visa's work limit` IF
        `my last visa had a work condition in the 010.611(4) list`
    AND (NOT `I am in a class the Minister specified for 010.611(1)(c)`)
    AND (NOT `I was granted it for a compelling need to work`)

-- Condition 8105(1): "the holder must not engage in work in Australia for more than 40 hours a fortnight during any
-- fortnight when the holder's course of study or training is in session." (2A): "If the visa held is a Subclass 500
-- (Student) visa, or a bridging visa granted on the basis of a valid application for a Subclass 500 (Student) visa,
-- this clause applies as if the reference in subclause (1) to 40 hours were instead a reference to 48 hours."
-- (2)(b): the limit does not apply to a masters by research or doctoral student who has commenced. (3): "fortnight
-- means the period of 14 days commencing on a Monday."
DECLARE `Visa carrying condition 8105` IS ONE OF
    `a Student visa (subclass 500)`
    `a bridging visa granted on a Student visa application`
    `a bridging visa granted on another application`

@export How many hours a fortnight may I work while my course is in session under condition 8105?
GIVEN `the visa I hold` IS A `Visa carrying condition 8105` @desc The visa you hold that carries condition 8105
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours a fortnight may I work in session` IS
    CONSIDER `the visa I hold`
    WHEN `a bridging visa granted on another application` THEN 40
    OTHERWISE 48

@export Is my work limited while my course is in session under condition 8105?
GIVEN `I have started a masters by research or doctorate on this visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your student visa was granted for a masters by research or doctoral degree and you have started it
      `the work is a registered requirement of my course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is required by the course as registered on CRICOS
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work limited in session` IF
    (NOT `I have started a masters by research or doctorate on this visa`) AND (NOT `the work is a registered requirement of my course`)

§§ `s 82 -- which visa ends when another begins, or when I leave`

-- s 5(1): "substantive visa means a visa other than: (a) a bridging visa; or (b) a criminal justice visa; or (c) an
-- enforcement visa." s 82(2): "A substantive visa held by a non-citizen ceases to be in effect if another substantive
-- visa (other than a special purpose visa) for the non-citizen comes into effect." (3): "A bridging visa held by a
-- non-citizen ceases to be in effect if another visa (other than a special purpose visa or a maritime crew visa) for
-- the non-citizen comes into effect." The s 82(2AA) maritime crew exception is not encoded.
DECLARE `Kind of visa` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary substantive visa`
    `a special purpose visa`
    `a maritime crew visa`
    `a bridging visa`

GIVEN `k` IS A `Kind of visa`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is substantive` IF
    CONSIDER `k`
    WHEN `a bridging visa` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export Does the visa I hold end when my new visa comes into effect (s 82(2), (3))?
GIVEN `the visa I hold` IS A `Kind of visa` @desc The kind of visa you hold now
      `the new visa` IS A `Kind of visa` @desc The kind of visa that is coming into effect
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my visa end when the new one comes into effect` IF
        (    `is substantive` `the visa I hold`
         AND `is substantive` `the new visa`
         AND (NOT (`the new visa` EQUALS `a special purpose visa`)))
    OR  (    (`the visa I hold` EQUALS `a bridging visa`)
         AND (NOT (`the new visa` EQUALS `a special purpose visa`))
         AND (NOT (`the new visa` EQUALS `a maritime crew visa`)))

-- s 82(8): "A visa to remain in, but not re-enter, Australia that is granted to a non-citizen in Australia ceases to be
-- in effect if the holder leaves Australia." (6): a visa to travel to and enter Australia during a particular period
-- "ceases to be in effect if the holder leaves Australia after that period". 010.511 gives a Bridging A permission
-- only to "remain in Australia" (INFERENCE: so s 82(8) ends it on departure; travelling needs a Bridging B, not
-- encoded).
@export Does my visa end when I leave Australia (s 82(6), (8))?
GIVEN `my visa lets me re-enter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your visa is permission to travel to and re-enter Australia
      `it was granted to me in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the visa was granted while you were in Australia
      `I leave after its travel period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you leave Australia after the period in which the visa lets you travel has ended
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my visa end when I leave` IF
        ((NOT `my visa lets me re-enter`) AND `it was granted to me in Australia`)
    OR  (`my visa lets me re-enter` AND `I leave after its travel period has ended`)

-- s 82(5): "A visa to travel to and enter Australia (whether also a visa to remain in Australia) during a particular
-- period or until a particular date ceases to be in effect at the end of that period or on that date unless the holder
-- of the visa: (a) has entered Australia in that period or on or before that date; and (b) is in Australia at the end of
-- that period or on that date." Read literally it reaches a permanent visa with a travel period (cl 801.511) granted in
-- Australia to a holder who never leaves and so never "entered" in the period; whether the Act means that is not
-- answered by the text read here, and this rule applies the words as written.
@export Does my visa end when its travel period ends (s 82(5))?
GIVEN `I have entered Australia during the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have entered Australia on this visa during its travel period
      `I am in Australia when the period ends` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you will be in Australia on the day the travel period ends
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my visa end when its travel period ends` IF
    NOT (`I have entered Australia during the period` AND `I am in Australia when the period ends`)

§§ `Sch 2 Part 801; reg 1.03 -- the permanent partner visa (Priya, d033, d035)`

-- reg 1.03: "long-term partner relationship ... means a relationship between the applicant and another person, each as
-- the spouse or de facto partner of the other, that has continued: (a) if there is a dependent child (other than a
-- step-child) of both the applicant and the other person -- for not less than 2 years; or (b) in any other case -- for
-- not less than 3 years."
@export Was I in a long-term partner relationship when I applied (reg 1.03)?
GIVEN `years our relationship had lasted when I applied` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years you had been spouses or de facto partners when you applied
      `we have a dependent child together` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your partner have a dependent child of you both (not a step-child)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I in a long-term partner relationship` IF
        (`we have a dependent child together` AND `years our relationship had lasted when I applied` >= 2)
    OR  `years our relationship had lasted when I applied` >= 3

-- 801.221(2): "(a) the applicant is the holder of a Subclass 820 visa; and (b) the applicant continues to be sponsored
-- ... by: (i) the sponsoring partner ...; and (c) the applicant is the spouse or de facto partner of the sponsoring
-- partner; and (d) subject to subclauses (6A) and (7), at least 2 years have passed since the application was made."
-- (6A): "(2)(d) ... do[es] not apply to an applicant who at the time of making the application was in a long-term
-- partner relationship with the sponsoring partner." (5): the sponsoring partner has died and the Minister is
-- satisfied the relationship would have continued. (6): the relationship has ceased and family violence by the
-- sponsoring partner, or a child custody, contact or maintenance link. (7): neither (5) nor (6) needs the 2 years.
-- 801.223, 801.226: public interest criteria, asked as one fact.
DECLARE `Permanent partner facts` HAS
    `I hold the temporary partner visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my partner still sponsors me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am still my partner's spouse or de facto partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years since I applied` IS A NUMBER
    `years our relationship had lasted when I applied` IS A NUMBER
    `we have a dependent child together` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my partner has died and we would have stayed together` IS A BOOLEAN
    `we separated after family violence by my partner, or with a child order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I meet the public interest criteria` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Do I meet the permanent partner visa criteria (cl 801.221)?
GIVEN `f` IS A `Permanent partner facts` @desc Facts about you, your partner and your temporary partner visa
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the permanent partner visa criteria` IF
        `f`'s `I hold the temporary partner visa`
    AND `f`'s `I meet the public interest criteria`
    AND (    (    `f`'s `my partner still sponsors me`
              AND `f`'s `I am still my partner's spouse or de facto partner`
              AND (    `f`'s `years since I applied` >= 2
                   OR  `Was I in a long-term partner relationship` (`f`'s `years our relationship had lasted when I applied`) (`f`'s `we have a dependent child together`)))
         OR  `f`'s `my partner has died and we would have stayed together`
         OR  `f`'s `we separated after family violence by my partner, or with a child order`)

-- reg 1.03: "Australian permanent resident means: (a) in relation to an applicant for a Return (Residence) (Class BB)
-- visa -- a non-citizen who is the holder of a permanent visa; or (b) in any other case ... -- a non-citizen who, being
-- usually resident in Australia, is the holder of a permanent visa."
@export Am I an Australian permanent resident (reg 1.03)?
GIVEN `I hold a permanent visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a permanent visa
      `I am usually resident in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you usually live in Australia
      `the question is for a resident return visa application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are asking for the purpose of applying for a resident return visa
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an Australian permanent resident` IF
    `I hold a permanent visa` AND (`I am usually resident in Australia` OR `the question is for a resident return visa application`)

§§ `ss 79, 81(2), 82(5), (6); cl 801.511; Sch 1 item 1128; Sch 2 Part 155 -- leaving and coming back (Priya, d035)`

-- 801.511: "Permanent visa permitting the holder to travel to and enter Australia for 5 years from date of grant."
@export For how many years from its grant may I travel on my permanent partner visa (cl 801.511)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many years may I travel on my permanent partner visa` IS 5

-- s 79: "If the holder of a visa leaves Australia the holder may only re-enter Australia because of the visa if: (a)
-- the visa is permission for the re-entry; and (b) the visa is in effect on re-entry." s 81(2): "A visa to enter
-- Australia within a period is not permission to so enter outside that period." s 82(6): such a visa ceases if the
-- holder leaves after the period. Times are counted in years from the visa's grant.
@export May I come back to Australia on my visa after this trip (ss 79, 81(2), 82(6))?
GIVEN `my visa lets me re-enter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your visa is permission to travel to and re-enter Australia
      `years of travel my visa gives` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years from grant your visa lets you travel to and enter Australia
      `years after grant I leave` IS A NUMBER @desc How long after the grant you leave Australia, in years
      `years after grant I return` IS A NUMBER @desc How long after the grant you will come back, in years
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I come back on my visa` IF
        `my visa lets me re-enter`
    AND `years after grant I leave` <= `years of travel my visa gives`
    AND `years after grant I return` <= `years of travel my visa gives`

@export Do I need a resident return visa to come back from this trip (ss 79, 81(2); cl 801.511)?
GIVEN `I hold a permanent visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a permanent visa
      `years of travel my visa gives` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years from grant your permanent visa lets you travel (5 for a partner visa)
      `years after grant I leave` IS A NUMBER @desc How long after the grant you leave Australia, in years
      `years after grant I return` IS A NUMBER @desc How long after the grant you will come back, in years
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I need a resident return visa` IF
        `I hold a permanent visa`
    AND (NOT (`May I come back on my visa` TRUE `years of travel my visa gives` `years after grant I leave` `years after grant I return`))

-- 155.211: the applicant "(a) is an Australian permanent resident; or (b) was an Australian citizen but has
-- subsequently lost or renounced Australian citizenship; or (c) is a former Australian permanent resident, other than
-- [one] whose most recent permanent visa was cancelled." 155.212(2): "lawfully present in Australia for a period of,
-- or periods that total, not less than 2 years in the period of 5 years immediately before the application ... and,
-- during that time, the applicant: (a) was: (i) the holder of a permanent visa; or (ii) an Australian citizen; and (b)
-- was not the holder of: (i) a temporary visa ...; or (ii) a bridging visa." (3) outside Australia and (3A) in
-- Australia: "the Minister is satisfied that the applicant has substantial business, cultural, employment or personal
-- ties with Australia which are of benefit to Australia" and has not been absent for a continuous 5 years (unless
-- compelling reasons). 155.511: "(b) if the applicant met the requirements of clause 155.211 and subclause 155.212(2)
-- at the time of application -- a period of 5 years from the date of grant; or (c) in any other case: (i) a period of
-- one year from the date of the grant; or (ii) a shorter period determined by the Minister." The family-unit route
-- (155.212(4)) and the decision criteria (special return criterion 5001, public interest criterion 4021) are not
-- encoded; 0 means not eligible on these facts. The Minister's shorter period is not encoded (1 is the most).
DECLARE `Resident return facts` HAS
    `I hold a permanent visa, or lost my citizenship, or my last permanent visa ended without cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years in the last 5 I was here as a permanent visa holder or citizen` IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister is satisfied I have substantial ties of benefit to Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have been away for 5 continuous years without compelling reasons` IS A BOOLEAN

@export How many years of travel would a resident return visa give me (cll 155.211, 155.212, 155.511)?
GIVEN `f` IS A `Resident return facts` @desc Facts about your residence and ties
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many years would a resident return visa give me` IS
    IF (NOT `f`'s `I hold a permanent visa, or lost my citizenship, or my last permanent visa ended without cancellation`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `f`'s `years in the last 5 I was here as a permanent visa holder or citizen` >= 2
         THEN 5
         ELSE IF `f`'s `the Minister is satisfied I have substantial ties of benefit to Australia` AND (NOT `f`'s `I have been away for 5 continuous years without compelling reasons`)
              THEN 1
              ELSE 0

-- Sch 1 item 1128(2)(a): "the base application charge ... is: (i) for an applicant who holds a valid passport issued by
-- a Pacific-regional country -- $505; or (ii) for any other applicant -- $1 475". Surcharges under reg 2.12C are not
-- encoded.
@export What is the base charge to apply for a resident return visa, in dollars (Sch 1 item 1128)?
GIVEN `I hold a Pacific-regional passport` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a valid passport issued by a Pacific-regional country
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the resident return visa charge` IS
    IF `I hold a Pacific-regional passport` THEN 505 ELSE 1475

§§ `ss 116, 117, 119, 128 -- can my visa be cancelled`

-- s 116(1): "the Minister may cancel a visa if he or she is satisfied that: (a) the decision to grant the visa was
-- based, wholly or partly, on a particular fact or circumstance that is no longer the case ...; or (aa) ... did not
-- exist; or (b) its holder has not complied with a condition of the visa; ... (e) the presence of its holder in
-- Australia is or may be ... a risk to ... the health, safety or good order of the Australian community ...; or (f)
-- the visa should not have been granted because the application for it or its grant was in contravention of this Act
-- ...; or (g) a prescribed ground for cancelling a visa applies". (1AA): not satisfied as to identity. (1AB):
-- incorrect information given by or on behalf of the holder was taken into account. (1AC): "a benefit was asked for or
-- received by, or ... offered or provided by, or on behalf of, the person ... in return for the occurrence of a
-- sponsorship-related event". (2): not if prescribed circumstances say not to cancel. (3): must if prescribed
-- circumstances say so (not encoded). s 117(2): "A permanent visa cannot be cancelled under subsection 116(1) if the
-- holder of the visa: (a) is in the migration zone; and (b) was immigration cleared on last entering Australia." The
-- bar names subsection (1) only, so it does not reach (1AA), (1AB) or (1AC). Grounds (c), (d) and (fa) are not
-- encoded.
DECLARE `Cancellation ground` IS ONE OF
    `a fact my visa was granted on no longer exists`
    `a fact my visa was granted on never existed`
    `I have not complied with a condition of my visa`
    `my presence is a risk to the community or a person`
    `my visa was granted in breach of the law`
    `a prescribed ground applies to me`
    `the Minister is not satisfied of my identity`
    `incorrect information given for me was relied on`
    `a benefit was asked or given for my sponsorship`

GIVEN `g` IS A `Cancellation ground`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a s 116(1) ground` IF
    CONSIDER `g`
    WHEN `the Minister is not satisfied of my identity` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `incorrect information given for me was relied on` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a benefit was asked or given for my sponsorship` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export May my visa be cancelled on this ground under s 116 (ss 116, 117(2))?
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Cancellation ground` @desc The ground the Minister relies on
      `the Minister is satisfied it exists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is satisfied that the ground exists
      `prescribed circumstances bar cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether circumstances prescribed under s 116(2) say the visa is not to be cancelled
      `I hold a permanent visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the visa is a permanent visa
      `I am in the migration zone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in Australia
      `I was immigration cleared when I last entered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were immigration cleared when you last entered Australia
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my visa be cancelled under s 116` IF
        `the Minister is satisfied it exists`
    AND (NOT `prescribed circumstances bar cancellation`)
    AND (NOT (    `is a s 116(1) ground` `the ground`
              AND `I hold a permanent visa`
              AND `I am in the migration zone`
              AND `I was immigration cleared when I last entered`))

-- s 119(1): "Subject to Subdivision F ..., if the Minister is considering cancelling a visa ... under section 116, the
-- Minister must, in writing, notify the holder that there appear to be grounds for cancelling it and: (a) give
-- particulars of those grounds and of the information ...; and (b) invite the holder to show within a specified time
-- that: (i) those grounds do not exist; or (ii) there is a reason why it should not be cancelled." s 128: if the
-- non-citizen is outside Australia and the Minister is satisfied "it is appropriate to cancel in accordance with this
-- Subdivision", the Minister "may, without notice to the holder of the visa, cancel the visa" (s 129: notice after).
@export Must I be told the grounds and invited to answer before my visa is cancelled under s 116 (ss 119, 128)?
GIVEN `I am outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are outside Australia
      `the Minister proceeds under s 128` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister, being satisfied it is appropriate, cancels under s 128 without prior notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be told before cancellation` IF
    NOT (`I am outside Australia` AND `the Minister proceeds under s 128`)

§§ `Sch 1 item 1240; reg 2.75 -- applying for a Skills in Demand visa (the engineer from Chennai, d047)`

-- Sch 1 item 1240(3): "(c) An applicant ... may be in or outside Australia, but not in immigration clearance. (d) An
-- applicant in Australia must hold: (i) a substantive visa; or (ii) a Subclass 010 (Bridging A) visa; or (iii) a
-- Subclass 020 (Bridging B) visa; or (iv) a Subclass 030 (Bridging C) visa. ... (f) If the applicant seeks to satisfy
-- the primary criteria ...: (i) a person must have nominated a proposed occupation ... in a stream; and (ii) the
-- application must be for a Subclass 482 ... visa in the stream for which the nominated occupation was nominated; and
-- (iii) the application must identify the nomination; and (iv) one of the following must apply: (A) the nomination has
-- been approved under section 140GB of the Act and the approval of the nomination has not ceased under regulation 2.75;
-- (B) a decision in respect of the nomination has not been made ...; and (v) the person who made the nomination must not
-- be the subject of a bar under section 140M". The skills-assessment rule in (g) is not encoded.
DECLARE `Skills in Demand application` HAS
    `an occupation has been nominated for me in a stream` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I apply in the stream it was nominated for` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my application identifies the nomination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the nomination is approved and its approval has not ceased, or is undecided` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my nominator is barred under s 140M` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am in immigration clearance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I hold a substantive visa or a Bridging A, B or C visa` IS A BOOLEAN

@export May I make a valid application for a Skills in Demand visa (Sch 1 item 1240)?
GIVEN `a` IS A `Skills in Demand application` @desc Facts about your nomination and where you are
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply for a Skills in Demand visa` IF
        `a`'s `an occupation has been nominated for me in a stream`
    AND `a`'s `I apply in the stream it was nominated for`
    AND `a`'s `my application identifies the nomination`
    AND `a`'s `the nomination is approved and its approval has not ceased, or is undecided`
    AND (NOT `a`'s `my nominator is barred under s 140M`)
    AND (NOT `a`'s `I am in immigration clearance`)
    AND ((NOT `a`'s `I am in Australia`) OR `a`'s `I hold a substantive visa or a Bridging A, B or C visa`)

-- reg 2.75(2): "An approval of a nomination ceases on the earliest of: ... (b) 12 months after the day on which the
-- nomination is approved unless, at that time, there is a visa application made by the nominee on the basis of the
-- nomination that has not been finally determined; ... (c) the day on which the nominee is granted a ... Subclass 482
-- (Skills in Demand) visa". Paragraphs (a) and (ba)-(g) (withdrawal, sponsor's status, work agreement) are not encoded.
@export Has the approval of my nomination run out before I applied (reg 2.75(2)(b))?
GIVEN `months since the nomination was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months ago the nomination was approved
      `I have an undecided application on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made a visa application on the nomination that is not finally determined
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my nomination approval run out` IF
    `months since the nomination was approved` >= 12 AND (NOT `I have an undecided application on it`)

-- Sch 1 item 1240(2)(a)(iii): "for any other applicant: ... Base application charge $4 015"; (ii): $3 290 for a holder
-- of a passport issued by a Pacific-regional country.
@export What is the base charge to apply for a Skills in Demand visa, in dollars (Sch 1 item 1240)?
GIVEN `I hold a Pacific-regional passport` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a valid passport issued by a Pacific-regional country
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the Skills in Demand visa charge` IS
    IF `I hold a Pacific-regional passport` THEN 3290 ELSE 4015

§§ `reg 1.03, 2.72(8), (15), 5.42A -- is my pay high enough (d047)`

-- reg 1.03: "core skills income threshold means $73,150." "specialist skills income threshold means $135,000." reg
-- 5.42A(1): "If the indexation factor for an indexation day is greater than 1, the dollar amounts ... are, on that day,
-- replaced by the amounts worked out" from AWOTE; "indexation day means the first 1 July to occur after the
-- commencement of this regulation and each later 1 July"; (5): the new amount is published on the Department's website.
-- The amount in force after 1 July 2025 is not in the text: it is an input, and since an amount is replaced only when
-- the factor is greater than 1 it can never fall below the figure in reg 1.03 (INFERENCE from (1); the text
-- deposited still prints the base figures). Enter 0 if you do not know it.
DECLARE `Stream` IS ONE OF
    `Specialist Skills`
    `Core Skills`
    `Labour Agreement`

@export What is the income threshold for my stream, in dollars a year (regs 1.03, 5.42A)?
GIVEN `the stream` IS A `Stream` @desc The stream your occupation is nominated in
      `the indexed threshold published for this year` IS A NUMBER @desc The threshold the Department has published for the current year, or 0 if you do not know it
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the income threshold for my stream` IS
    CONSIDER `the stream`
    WHEN `Specialist Skills` THEN IF `the indexed threshold published for this year` > 135000 THEN `the indexed threshold published for this year` ELSE 135000
    WHEN `Core Skills` THEN IF `the indexed threshold published for this year` > 73150 THEN `the indexed threshold published for this year` ELSE 73150
    OTHERWISE 0

-- reg 2.72(15): for the Specialist Skills or Core Skills stream, if "(b) the Minister is not satisfied that the
-- nominee's annual earnings ... will be at least the amount specified by the Minister in a legislative instrument made
-- for the purposes of this paragraph", the Minister must be satisfied that "(d) the annual market salary rate,
-- excluding any non-monetary benefits, for the occupation ... is not less than [the threshold for the stream]; and (e)
-- the nominee's annual earnings ... will not be less than the annual market salary rate ...; and (f) the nominee's
-- annual earnings, excluding any non-monetary benefits, ... will not be less than [the threshold]". The market rate is
-- set by the sponsor under a method in an instrument (2.72(17)): an input. (16) lets the Minister disregard (d), (e) or
-- (f) when reasonable: not encoded. The Labour Agreement stream is outside (15); its terms are in the work agreement,
-- so TRUE here means only that reg 2.72(15) does not stop the nomination.
@export Is my pay high enough for my nomination (reg 2.72(15))?
GIVEN `the stream` IS A `Stream` @desc The stream your occupation is nominated in
      `my annual earnings excluding non-monetary benefits` IS A NUMBER @desc What you will earn a year in money, not counting non-monetary benefits
      `the annual market salary rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The annual market salary rate for the occupation, as the sponsor determined it
      `the indexed threshold published for this year` IS A NUMBER @desc The threshold the Department has published for the current year, or 0 if you do not know it
      `the Minister is satisfied I earn at least the exemption amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is satisfied you will earn at least the amount in the instrument for reg 2.72(15)(b)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my pay high enough for my nomination` IF
    CONSIDER `the stream`
    WHEN `Labour Agreement` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE
            `the Minister is satisfied I earn at least the exemption amount`
        OR  (    `the annual market salary rate` >= `What is the income threshold for my stream` `the stream` `the indexed threshold published for this year`
             AND `my annual earnings excluding non-monetary benefits` >= `the annual market salary rate`
             AND `my annual earnings excluding non-monetary benefits` >= `What is the income threshold for my stream` `the stream` `the indexed threshold published for this year`)

-- reg 2.72(8)(a): for the Specialist Skills stream, "(i) the occupation and its corresponding 6-digit code correspond
-- to an occupation and its corresponding 6-digit code that is specified in Major Group 1, 2, 4, 5 or 6 in ANZSCO"
-- (so not trades, Major Group 3, nor machinery operators or labourers, 7 and 8). The Core Skills stream uses the
-- occupation list in the 2.72(9) instrument (not deposited).
@export Is my occupation in an ANZSCO major group the Specialist Skills stream allows (reg 2.72(8)(a))?
GIVEN `the ANZSCO major group of my occupation` IS A NUMBER @desc The first digit of your occupation's ANZSCO code (1 to 8)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my occupation open to the Specialist Skills stream` IF
        `the ANZSCO major group of my occupation` EQUALS 1
    OR  `the ANZSCO major group of my occupation` EQUALS 2
    OR  `the ANZSCO major group of my occupation` EQUALS 4
    OR  `the ANZSCO major group of my occupation` EQUALS 5
    OR  `the ANZSCO major group of my occupation` EQUALS 6

§§ `Sch 2 Part 482 -- the Skills in Demand visa criteria and its term (d047)`

-- 482.211: if in Australia, substantial compliance with the conditions of the last substantive visa and any later
-- bridging visa. 482.212: "(1)(a) the nomination ... has been approved under section 140GB ...; (b) the person who made
-- the nomination was an approved work sponsor at the time the nomination was approved; (c) the approval of the
-- nomination has not ceased under regulation 2.75. (2) ... (a) the applicant's intention to perform the nominated
-- occupation is genuine; (b) the position ... is genuine." 482.213: no contravention of s 245AR(1), 245AS(1), 245AT(1)
-- or 245AU(1) in the previous 3 years, unless "the Minister considers that it is reasonable to disregard the conduct".
-- 482.214: "adequate arrangements for health insurance". 482.216: no adverse information about the nominator, or it is
-- reasonable to disregard it. 482.217, 482.218: public interest and special return criteria (one fact). For the
-- Specialist Skills (482.221-482.223) and Core Skills (482.231-482.233) streams alike: "at least 12 months full-time
-- work" in the nominated occupation or a related field "during the period of 5 years ending immediately before the day
-- the application was made"; the skills, qualifications and employment background the Minister considers necessary;
-- the language test requirements; and "the applicant is employed to work in the nominated occupation" in "the
-- person's business or a business of an associated entity of the person" (unless a 2.72(13) occupation). 482.215
-- (medical practitioners), the overseas business sponsor variant and the Labour Agreement stream are not encoded.
DECLARE `Skills in Demand criteria` HAS
    `I am in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I substantially complied with my last visas' conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the nomination is approved, by an approved sponsor, and has not ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my intention and the position are genuine` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I paid or took a benefit for sponsorship in the last 3 years` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister disregards that conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have adequate health insurance arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is no adverse information about my nominator, or it is disregarded` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I meet the public interest and special return criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of full-time work in the occupation in the last 5 years` IS A NUMBER
    `the Minister considers I have the skills needed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I meet the language requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am employed in the occupation in the sponsor's business or an associate's` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Do I meet the Skills in Demand visa criteria in the Specialist Skills or Core Skills stream (cll 482.211-482.233)?
GIVEN `c` IS A `Skills in Demand criteria` @desc Facts about you, your work history and your nomination
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the Skills in Demand criteria` IF
        ((NOT `c`'s `I am in Australia`) OR `c`'s `I substantially complied with my last visas' conditions`)
    AND `c`'s `the nomination is approved, by an approved sponsor, and has not ceased`
    AND `c`'s `my intention and the position are genuine`
    AND ((NOT `c`'s `I paid or took a benefit for sponsorship in the last 3 years`) OR `c`'s `the Minister disregards that conduct`)
    AND `c`'s `I have adequate health insurance arrangements`
    AND `c`'s `there is no adverse information about my nominator, or it is disregarded`
    AND `c`'s `I meet the public interest and special return criteria`
    AND `c`'s `months of full-time work in the occupation in the last 5 years` >= 12
    AND `c`'s `the Minister considers I have the skills needed`
    AND `c`'s `I meet the language requirements`
    AND `c`'s `I am employed in the occupation in the sponsor's business or an associate's`

-- 482.511(1), table item 1: for a primary applicant, the visa period ends at "the end of the period of stay proposed in
-- the nomination identified in the application for the visa, starting on the date of grant of the visa"; item 2: "the
-- end of the period of 5 years" for the holder of a Hong Kong passport of a specified class or a British National
-- (Overseas) passport. The secondary applicants' items 3-5 are not encoded.
@export For how many years may I stay on my Skills in Demand visa (cl 482.511)?
GIVEN `years of stay proposed in my nomination` IS A NUMBER @desc The period of stay your sponsor proposed in the nomination, in years
      `I hold a specified Hong Kong or a British National (Overseas) passport` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the date of grant, you hold a Hong Kong passport of a specified class or a British National (Overseas) passport
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many years may I stay on my Skills in Demand visa` IS
    IF `I hold a specified Hong Kong or a British National (Overseas) passport` THEN 5 ELSE `years of stay proposed in my nomination`

§§ `s 41; Sch 2 cll 482.611-482.613; Sch 8 conditions 8501, 8607 -- the conditions I must keep (d047)`

-- 482.611: "If the applicant satisfies the primary criteria for the grant of the visa, condition 8607 must be imposed."
-- 8607(1): "The holder must work only in the occupation (the nominated occupation) nominated by the nomination
-- identified in the application for the most recent Subclass 482 (Skills in Demand) visa granted to the holder." (2)(c):
-- in the Specialist Skills or Core Skills stream with a nominator that was not an overseas business sponsor, "work only
-- in a position in the person's business or a business of an associated entity of the person". (3): (2) does not apply
-- if "(a) the nominated occupation is an occupation specified by the Minister in an instrument made under subregulation
-- 2.72(13); or (b) the holder is continuing to work for a person for the purpose of fulfilling a requirement under a
-- law relating to industrial relations and relating to the giving of notice."
@export May I do this work without breaching condition 8607 (cl 8607(1)-(3))?
GIVEN `the work is in my nominated occupation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is in the occupation your sponsor nominated
      `the work is in my sponsor's business or an associated entity's` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the position is in your sponsor's business or a business of an associated entity
      `my occupation is specified under reg 2.72(13)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your occupation is one the Minister has specified under reg 2.72(13)
      `I am working out notice for a former employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are working for someone only to give the notice an industrial relations law requires
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I do this work under condition 8607` IF
        `the work is in my nominated occupation`
    AND (   `the work is in my sponsor's business or an associated entity's`
         OR `my occupation is specified under reg 2.72(13)`
         OR `I am working out notice for a former employer`)

-- 8607(4): "the holder must commence work within: (a) if the holder was outside Australia when the visa was granted --
-- 90 days after the holder's arrival in Australia; or (b) if the holder was in Australia when the visa was granted --
-- 90 days after the holder's visa was granted."
@export Within how many days must I start work on my Skills in Demand visa (cl 8607(4))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Within how many days must I start work` IS 90

-- 8607(5): "The holder may cease to work in accordance with subclauses (1) and (2) for a period, but: (a) any such
-- period must not exceed 180 consecutive days; and (b) the total number of days on which the holder does not work in
-- accordance with subclauses (1) and (2) must not exceed 365 during the visa period".
@export Have I stayed within the time condition 8607 lets me be without sponsored work (cl 8607(5))?
GIVEN `my longest run of days without sponsored work` IS A NUMBER @desc The longest unbroken run of days you have not been working in line with 8607
      `my total days without sponsored work on this visa` IS A NUMBER @desc All the days on this visa you have not been working in line with 8607
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I within the time I may be without sponsored work` IF
    `my longest run of days without sponsored work` <= 180 AND `my total days without sponsored work on this visa` <= 365

-- 482.612: "Condition 8501 must be imposed." 8501: "The holder must maintain adequate arrangements for health insurance
-- while the holder is in Australia."
@export Must I keep adequate health insurance while I am in Australia on my Skills in Demand visa (cl 482.612; condition 8501)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I keep health insurance` IS TRUE

§§ `regs 2.79, 2.80, 2.87 -- what my sponsor owes me (d047)`

-- reg 2.79(3)(b): for a nomination made on or after 18 March 2018, the sponsor "must ensure that: (i) the primary
-- sponsored person's annual earnings ... are not less than the annual earnings the person indicated, at the time the
-- nomination was approved, would be provided ...; and (ii) ... not less than the earnings an Australian citizen or an
-- Australian permanent resident earns or would earn for performing equivalent work in the same workplace at the same
-- location; and (iii) the employment conditions (other than in relation to earnings) ... are no less favourable".
-- (1A): it "does not apply ... if ... (b) the annual earnings of the primary sponsored person are equal to or greater
-- than the amount specified by the Minister in an instrument in writing for this paragraph". (4): it runs from the
-- nomination's approval (or the visa's grant) until the earlier of a further substantive visa that is not a 482 (or 457)
-- and "the day on which the primary sponsored person ceases employment with the person".
@export Must my sponsor pay me at least the nominated salary and what an Australian earns for the same work (reg 2.79)?
GIVEN `I still work for my sponsor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are still employed by your sponsor
      `I have been granted a further visa other than a 482` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since been granted another substantive visa (not a 482 or 457) that is in effect
      `I earn at least the amount in the reg 2.79(1A) instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your annual earnings reach the amount the Minister specified for reg 2.79(1A)(b)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my sponsor pay me the equivalent terms` IF
        `I still work for my sponsor`
    AND (NOT `I have been granted a further visa other than a 482`)
    AND (NOT `I earn at least the amount in the reg 2.79(1A) instrument`)

-- reg 2.80(1)(e), (2): a standard business sponsor of a 482 holder "must pay the travel costs of the primary sponsored
-- person ... (a) if the costs have been requested in writing by: ... (ii) the primary sponsored person ...; and (b) that
-- have not already been paid ...; and (c) that are reasonable and necessary." (3)(d): the request must be made while the
-- person holds the 482. (4): economy class to the country named, paid within 30 days of the request, is taken to be
-- reasonable and necessary. (5)(b): the duty ends when another sponsor's nomination of me is approved, or I am granted
-- a further substantive visa of a different subclass, or I have left Australia and the visa has ceased.
@export Must my sponsor pay my fare home (reg 2.80)?
GIVEN `I asked in writing while holding the visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you asked your sponsor in writing for your travel costs while you held the Skills in Demand visa
      `the costs have already been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the sponsor has already paid them
      `the costs are reasonable and necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the costs are reasonable and necessary (economy class to your passport country is)
      `another sponsor's nomination of me has been approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another approved sponsor's nomination of you has been approved
      `I have been granted a visa of a different subclass` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been granted a further substantive visa of a different subclass that is in effect
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my sponsor pay my fare home` IF
        `I asked in writing while holding the visa`
    AND (NOT `the costs have already been paid`)
    AND `the costs are reasonable and necessary`
    AND (NOT `another sponsor's nomination of me has been approved`)
    AND (NOT `I have been granted a visa of a different subclass`)

-- reg 2.87(1A), (1B): a person who "is or was an approved work sponsor" must not transfer to another person, have
-- another person pay it, or recover or seek to recover from another person, "some or all of the costs, including
-- migration agent costs: (i) associated with the person becoming an approved work sponsor; or (ii) associated with
-- the person being an approved work sponsor; ... (iiia) associated with a nomination under subsection 140GB(1) of the
-- Act (including a fee ... or nomination training contribution charge); or (iv) that relate specifically to the
-- recruitment of [the primary sponsored person or a non-citizen] for the purposes of a nomination". The worker's own
-- visa application charge is not in the list (INFERENCE: reg 2.87 does not forbid passing it on; other law may).
DECLARE `Cost` IS ONE OF
    `the cost of my sponsor becoming or being a sponsor`
    `the nomination fee or training contribution charge`
    `the cost of recruiting me for the nomination`
    `my own visa application charge`

@export Does reg 2.87 forbid my sponsor to pass this cost on to me?
GIVEN `the cost` IS A `Cost` @desc The cost your sponsor wants you to bear
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does reg 2.87 forbid passing this cost to me` IF
    CONSIDER `the cost`
    WHEN `my own visa application charge` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `ss 5(1), 140E, 140GB, 140H, 140Q, 486R(5) -- my sponsor's approval and what it risks (d047)`

-- s 140E(1): "The Minister must approve a person as a work sponsor ... if prescribed criteria are satisfied." s 5(1):
-- "approved work sponsor means: (a) a person: (i) who has been approved under section 140E as a work sponsor ...; and
-- (ii) whose approval has not been cancelled under section 140M, or otherwise ceased to have effect under section 140G
-- ...; or (b) a person (other than a Minister) who is a party to a work agreement."
@export Is my employer an approved work sponsor (s 5(1); s 140E)?
GIVEN `my employer was approved under s 140E` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has been approved as a work sponsor under s 140E
      `the approval has been cancelled or has ceased` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that approval has been cancelled (s 140M) or has ceased (s 140G)
      `my employer is a party to a work agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer (not a Minister) is a party to a labour agreement with the Minister
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employer an approved work sponsor` IF
        (`my employer was approved under s 140E` AND (NOT `the approval has been cancelled or has ceased`))
    OR  `my employer is a party to a work agreement`

-- s 140GB(2): "The Minister must approve a person's nomination if: (a) in a case to which section 140GBA applies,
-- unless the person is exempt ... -- the labour market testing condition ... is satisfied; and (aa) ... the person has
-- paid the [nomination training contribution] charge; and (ab) in any case -- the person is an approved work sponsor;
-- and (b) in any case -- the prescribed criteria are satisfied." The prescribed criteria are reg 2.72 (the salary test
-- above is one of them); here they are one input, as the Minister is satisfied.
@export Must the Minister approve my sponsor's nomination of me (s 140GB(2))?
GIVEN `labour market testing is satisfied, exempt or not required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the labour market testing condition is satisfied, or your sponsor is exempt, or s 140GBA does not apply
      `the training contribution charge is paid or not payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any nomination training contribution charge has been paid
      `my sponsor is an approved work sponsor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your sponsor is an approved work sponsor
      `the reg 2.72 criteria are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is satisfied the criteria in reg 2.72 (occupation, genuine full-time position, salary, contract) are met
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my nomination be approved` IF
        `labour market testing is satisfied, exempt or not required`
    AND `the training contribution charge is paid or not payable`
    AND `my sponsor is an approved work sponsor`
    AND `the reg 2.72 criteria are satisfied`

-- s 140H(1): "A person who is or was an approved sponsor must satisfy the sponsorship obligations prescribed by the
-- regulations" (so regs 2.79 and 2.80 bind a former sponsor too, within their own end dates). s 140Q(1): "Civil
-- penalty: (a) if the person is an approved work sponsor -- 240 penalty units; or (b) in any other case -- 60 penalty
-- units." s 486R(5): the order "must not be more than: (a) if the person is a body corporate -- 5 times the amount ...
-- specified for the civil penalty provision".
@export What is the most my sponsor can be ordered to pay for breaking a sponsorship obligation, in penalty units (ss 140Q(1), 486R(5))?
GIVEN `my sponsor is still an approved work sponsor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your sponsor is still an approved work sponsor (not a former one)
      `my sponsor is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your sponsor is a body corporate
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most my sponsor can be ordered to pay` IS
    IF `my sponsor is still an approved work sponsor`
    THEN (IF `my sponsor is a company` THEN 5 * 240 ELSE 240)
    ELSE (IF `my sponsor is a company` THEN 5 * 60 ELSE 60)

§§ `ss 245AQ, 245AS, 245AB, 245AC, 245AG -- what I must not do, and working without the right visa (d047)`

-- s 245AG(2): "a person allows a person to work if, and only if: (a) the first person employs the second person under a
-- contract of service; or (b) the first person engages the second person, other than in a domestic context, under a
-- contract for services; or (ba) the first person participates in an arrangement ... for the performance of work by
-- the second person ...; ... or (e) the prescribed circumstances exist." Paragraphs (c) and (d) are not encoded.
@export Does the person I work for "allow me to work" under s 245AG?
GIVEN `they employ me under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they employ you as an employee
      `they engage me under a contract for services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they engage you as a contractor
      `it is in a domestic context` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a contractor engagement is in a domestic (household) context
      `they take part in an arrangement for my work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they take part in an arrangement for you to work, such as a labour hire chain
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do they allow me to work` IF
        `they employ me under a contract of service`
    OR  (`they engage me under a contract for services` AND (NOT `it is in a domestic context`))
    OR  `they take part in an arrangement for my work`

-- s 245AS(1): "A person (the first person) contravenes this subsection if: (a) the first person offers to provide, or
-- provides, a benefit to another person (the second person); and (b) the first person offers to provide, or provides,
-- the benefit in return for the occurrence of a sponsorship-related event. Civil penalty: 240 penalty units." (2):
-- "even if the sponsorship-related event does not occur". (3): not "if the benefit is a payment of a reasonable amount
-- for a professional service". s 245AQ: a sponsorship-related event includes a nomination under s 140GB, an employer
-- employing a person in a sponsored occupation, and "the grant of a sponsored visa". The same conduct is a ground for
-- cancelling my visa (s 116(1AC)) and bars a 482 for 3 years unless disregarded (482.213).
@export Would I contravene s 245AS by offering or giving something for my sponsorship?
GIVEN `I offer or give a benefit for a sponsorship-related event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you offer or give money or another benefit in return for a nomination, sponsorship, job or visa grant (whether or not it happens)
      `it is a reasonable payment for a professional service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is only a reasonable payment for a professional service, such as a migration agent's fee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would I contravene s 245AS` IF
    `I offer or give a benefit for a sponsorship-related event` AND (NOT `it is a reasonable payment for a professional service`)

@export What is the most I can be ordered to pay for contravening s 245AS, in penalty units?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be ordered to pay under s 245AS` IS 240

-- s 245AB(1): a person contravenes it if "(a) the first person allows, or continues to allow, another person (the
-- worker) to work; and (b) the worker is an unlawful non-citizen." s 245AC(1): or the worker "(b) is a lawful
-- non-citizen; and (c) ... holds a visa that is subject to a work-related condition; and (d) ... is in breach of the
-- work-related condition solely because of doing the work". (2) of each: not if the first person "takes reasonable
-- steps at reasonable times to verify". These bind the employer; the worker's own exposure is losing lawful status
-- (s 14) or the visa (s 116(1)(b)). The old worker offence, s 235, is repealed (endnotes: "rep No 1, 2024").
@export Would my employer contravene s 245AB or s 245AC by letting me do this work?
GIVEN `I am an unlawful non-citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in Australia without a visa in effect
      `this work breaches a work condition of my visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether doing this work alone puts you in breach of a work-related condition of your visa
      `my employer took reasonable steps at reasonable times to check` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer took reasonable steps at reasonable times (for example, VEVO) to verify your status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would my employer contravene ss 245AB or 245AC` IF
    (`I am an unlawful non-citizen` OR `this work breaches a work condition of my visa`) AND (NOT `my employer took reasonable steps at reasonable times to check`)
